summary: D227's seq_cst between two CPU contexts, a process and its copy over a shared page, as each backend lowers it (D499): two seq_cst stores each followed by a seq_cst load of the other's word never both read the old values, in rounds whose starts are staggered; targeted where it runs on hardware or under an emulator that keeps seq_cst order, since QEMU does not keep arm64's stlr before ldar; it cannot show that the forbidden outcome would occur without the orderings, only that it was not seen
